Date-range membership: strengthen until the listed mutants die. Save /workspace/daterange.mjs:

export function inRange(dateIso, startIso, endIso) {
  // inclusive start, exclusive end; all 'YYYY-MM-DD'
  return dateIso >= startIso && dateIso < endIso;
}
export function rangesIntersect(aStart, aEnd, bStart, bEnd) {
  return aStart < bEnd && bStart < aEnd;
}

Current daterange.test.mjs (create it too, node:test): one test asserting inRange('2026-06-15','2026-06-01','2026-07-01') is true, one asserting rangesIntersect('2026-01-01','2026-02-01','2026-01-15','2026-03-01') is true. Kill list: M1: >= -> >. M2: < -> <= (in inRange). M3: && -> || (in inRange). M4/M5: each < -> <= in rangesIntersect. M6: bStart < aEnd -> bStart < aStart. Add boundary tests (a date equal to start; equal to end; adjacent ranges sharing exactly one endpoint must NOT intersect; fully disjoint; contained) until every mutant is killed. Verify with a mutate-and-run harness script (node, string replacement, temp files, spawn node --test) printing a results table; require 6/6 KILLED plus green pristine tests.

